# Story 91: View vs Control Mode (45s)
# Hook: View lets them watch. Control lets them type. You decide at share time.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-091-view-vs-control.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
View lets them watch. Control lets them type. You decide at share time.

[00:03.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh and double-Escape into rysh mode. Every share command takes an optional mode: view or control.

[00:09.0 --> 00:18.0]
##share pane view is the default. Remote users observe live output but cannot send any input -- read-only.

[00:18.0 --> 00:26.0]
##unshare pane stops it. Now ##share pane control grants full control: subscribers can send shell commands and prompts.

[00:26.0 --> 00:36.0]
##share status reflects the current mode. Control-mode commands are validated server-side against a blocklist.

[00:36.0 --> 00:42.0]
The default share mode also comes from your [upstream] config, so --shared sessions start in view unless you change it.

[00:42.0 --> 00:45.0]
View to demo, control to pair. The choice is yours, pane by pane.

